dh360d (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * daemon: report real radiator fan RPM instead of a hardcoded 0. The RPM
    fields were never populated, so the screen always showed 0000.
  * daemon: cap reported percentages at 99. The screen's percentage boxes are
    two characters wide and the firmware renders 100 as "FF".
  * service: drop After=multi-user.target. It made the start job wait on the
    whole boot transaction, so a hung plymouth-quit-wait.service could leave
    the driver queued and never dispatched. The udev rule's SYSTEMD_WANTS
    starts it when the CH340 enumerates.
  * packaging: ship systemd/dh360d.service from debian/rules too. A second,
    stale copy at debian/dh360d.service was shadowing it in debhelper builds.

 -- S. Eric Clark <25495882+clarkse@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 22:52:47 -0700

dh360d (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * CH340-based serial driver for the Darkflash DH360D AIO LCD.
  * CLI: detect, handshake, push, daemon, sniff.
  * systemd service streams live host sensors to the pump screen on boot.
  * udev rule for non-root access and a /dev/dh360d symlink.

